  "body": "This PR is partial. It fixes two of the three `known-fail #2849` pins. The third pin needs a maintainer decision.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `lead_ext::axis_reseat` keeps the ring start only when the first edge is exactly on X or Y, or when no edge is nearer an axis. Before, it kept the start for each first edge within `axis_tol` (1 degree).\n- `descent_xy::plan_xy` tries the first-cut tangent first, as before. When no radius fits and the first pass is a ring that returns to its start, it tries the direction of the closing edge. It uses that direction only within 1e-3 rad of the first-cut tangent.\n- The `known-fail #2849` markers of two `lead_approach` pins are removed. Their asserts do not change.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/2849-two-pins.md`.\n\nThis is the held work of `issue/2849-three-pins` (`bfc1dc03b`), taken onto the latest main and gated again.\n\n## Cause\n\n- Test 2: the solidcore mesh gives a first edge 0.93 degrees off X. That edge is inside the tolerance, so the start was kept. `entry_arc::true_arc` posts G18/G19 only for an exact axis edge, so the arc was posted as chords.\n- Test 1: the arc tangent came from the fitted walk arc. The ring polyline that returns to the start was 0.6 micron off that tangent line. The ring behind the start then crossed the arc hull on both sides, at each radius.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins (red on unchanged code, green with the fix):\n  - `lead_approach::an_axis_aligned_lead_start_posts_the_users_arc_entry_as_g18_or_g19`\n  - `lead_approach::the_horizontal_arc_entry_on_the_users_pocket_verifies_silent`\n- Unit pins: `lead_ext::reseat_tests` (2 tests), `descent_xy::closing_tests` (1 test).\n- Mutations:\n  - Old `lead_ext.rs`: the G18/G19 pin goes red. The other pins stay green.\n  - Old `descent_xy.rs`: the horizontal arc pin goes red. The other pins stay green.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): green. Steps: motion lib, `motion:xy_arc_entry`, `app:area_open`, `app:lead_approach`.\n- Also run and green:\n  - motion: `vertical_arc_entry`, `refusal_ghost`, `one_descent`, `level_links`, `entry_arc_3d`, `entry_approach`, `entry_arc`, `blind_floor`, `center_cut_law`, `corner_arc_radius`.\n  - app: `wall_arc_entry`, `top_plane_noise`, `solid_law_goldens`, `recorded_post_streams`, `level_links`, `contour_none_lead`, `arc_entry`, `golden_cl`, `contour_start_point`, `shoulder_adaptive`.\n  - post: `vertical_arc_entry`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Test 3 (`shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`) keeps its marker. A ring order change fixes it, but it makes `corner_arc_radius::the_crossing_law_keeps_the_arc_turns_and_crosses_nowhere` red. The two pins want opposite wall orders on a holed area. The maintainer decides the law (see the issue and the decision record).\n- The batch and release tiers did not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2831 touches `crates/app/tests/lead_approach.rs` (a mechanical sweep of many test files). It does not change the marker lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: The \"Axis start\" option posts the arc entry as G18/G19 when a fine chord is near an axis, and the horizontal arc entry fits on fine ring outlines where it was dropped before.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #2849\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
